 "title": "Geometric Algebra Applications, Vol. I: Computer Vision, Graphics and Neurocomputing",
 "byline": "Eduardo Bayro-Corrochano · Springer, 2019",
 "note": "Long and finely sectioned, so summaries and terms are given per chapter; each section is listed with its PDF page range. Exercise and conclusion sections and the front-matter guide are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A large reference on Clifford/geometric algebra as a unified language for geometric computing in robotics, vision and neural networks. Part I develops the mathematics: multivector products and operations, differentiation and multilinear functions, geometric calculus (including Maxwell and Dirac equations), Lie algebras and groups via rotors, 2D–4D algebras, kinematics with motors, conformal geometric algebra and higher algebras, plus implementation issues. Later parts cover quaternion and Clifford Fourier and wavelet transforms, geometric algebra for multi-view and stereo computer vision, geometric neural networks and Clifford SVMs, and applications: Lie filters, speech recognition, projective invariants and omnidirectional vision, tensor voting and Hough transforms in conformal algebra, medical data registration and surface reconstruction."
